Complete the task below in the current directory. Write each file with its own shell command, and run the shell command `sleep 3` between files, so every step is its own tool call. When done, answer with the list of files you wrote, one per line, and nothing else.

## task

{
  "name": "Complete six planet notes",
  "description": "Ensure planet1.txt through planet6.txt each contains exactly one sentence about Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn respectively. Existing filenames alone do not demonstrate the required content, and the recorded footer metadata is not evidence of sentence correctness.",
  "definition_of_done": "All six files exist and their complete contents are exactly one sentence each, with the planets matching the required order; this is demonstrated by inspecting the file contents, not merely their filenames.",
  "validation": {
    "command": "",
    "query": "Read all six files and confirm each contains exactly one sentence about the required planet in order."
  }
}
